          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+shape+for+higher+structures"} shape
            categories” such as Connes’
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cycles"} category of cycles
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal%27s+category+Gamma"} Segal's category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %em generalized Reedy category
            lifts this restriction, while maintaining the truth of the main theorem about Reedy categories: the existence of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
          %p
            In fact, there are two notions of generalized Reedy category in the literature. Cisinski’s “catégories squelletiques” (Ch. 8 in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Cisinski"}
                %em PCMH
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            %a{:href => "#BergerMoerdijk11"} Berger &amp; Moerdijk 2011
            are a strictly broader generalization suitable e.g. for describing
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#generalized_reedy_categories Generalized Reedy categories
          #BMGeneralizedReedyCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong Berger-Moerdijk generalized Reedy category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              together with two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategories"} wide subcategories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_+
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\colon ob(R)\to \alpha
              called
              = succeed "," do
                %em degree
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal"} ordinal
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  every non-isomorphism in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mo +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_+
                  raises degree,
              %li
                %p
                  every non-isomorphism in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mo −
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
                  lowers degree,
              %li
                %p
                  every isomorphism in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  preserves degree,
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mo +
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mo −
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_+\cap R_-
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  (equivalently, every isomorphism is in both
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mo +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_+
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mo −
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudomonic+functor"} pseudomonic
                  subcategories),
              %li
                %p
                  every morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  factors as a map in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mo −
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
                  followed by a map in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mo +
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_+
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mo −
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in R_-
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi θ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
                  is an isomorphism such that
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi θ
                          %mi f
                          %mo =
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta f = f
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi θ
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta = 1
                  (isomorphisms see the maps in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mo −
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
                  as
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epis
            %p
              The last condition implies that the isomorphism in the penultimate condition must be unique. It is not self-dual, but has an obvious dual version. A BM generalized Reedy category is said to be
              %strong dualizable
              if it satisfies both this condition and its dual.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              of generalized Reedy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to R
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              whish takes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_+
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_+
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_-
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
              and preserves the degree.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#BergerMoerdijk11"}> Berger &amp; Moerdijk 2011, def. 1.1
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Generalized Reedy category structures (as opposed to ordinary structures!) can always be transported along
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For a
              = succeed "," do
                %strong Cisinski generalized Reedy category
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BMGeneralizedReedyCategory"}
              is replaced by
            %ul
              %li
                every morphism in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
                admits a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
                are equal precisely when they have the same sections.
          %p
            For clarity, in the context of generalized Reedy categories, an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
            may be called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em strict Reedy category
          %h3#prima_facie_comparison_between_cisinski_and_bergermoerdijk Prima Facie comparison between Cisinski and Berger-Moerdijk.
          %p
            The only difference between the Cisinski notion and the Berger-Moerdijk notion is in the final condition – let’s say, between the
            %em Cisinski condition
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Berger-Moerdijk condition
          %p
            It’s easy to see that the Cisinski condition is
            %strong strictly stronger
            than the Berger-Moerdijk condition. The Berger-Moerdijk condition asks that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mo −
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
            arrows be something less than epimorphic in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mo −
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
            arrows be
            %em actually
            epimorphic in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %em split
            epimorphic, and more.
          %h3#presheaves_on_reedy_categories Presheaves on Reedy categories.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a generalized Reedy category, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-cells," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p (..)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#NormalMorphisms Normal monomorphisms (Cisinski)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a Cisinski generalized Reedy category.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              is called
              %em degenerate
              precisely if there is a non-isomorphism out of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_-
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski"}> Cisinski, prop. 8.1.9
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              there exists a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : a \to b
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_-
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              non-degenerate.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Cisisnki"}> Cisinski, prop. 8.1.13
            ).
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in X(a)
              is called
              %strong degenerate
              precisely if there is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : a \to a'
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_-
              and a cell
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in X(a')
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi u
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(\alpha) : u \mapsto v
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski"}> Cisinski, cor. 8.1.10
            ).
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/X
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              an
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in X(a)
              is called
              %strong dominant
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,v) \in A/X
              has trivial
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            %p
              An
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in X(a)
              is called
              %strong normal
              if there is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : a \to b
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_-
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              non-degenerate, and a dominant
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in X(b)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi v
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi u
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(\alpha) : v \mapsto u
                    \\,.
            %p
              The presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is called
              %strong normal
              if all its cells are normal.
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski"}> Cisinski, 8.1.23
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p A non-degenerate cell is normal precisely if it is dominant.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is normal precisely if all its non-degenerate cells are dominant.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski"}> Cisinski, cor. 8.1.25
            ).
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            be a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              The morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              is called
              %strong normal
              if every cell of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              not in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is normal.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski"}> Cisinski, 8.1.30
            ).
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              between normal presheaves is normal.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The class of normal monomorphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
              is closed under
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"}> pushouts
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"}> transfinite composition
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"}> retracts
                  \.
            %p
              In fact, the class of normal monomorphisms is that generated under these operations from the boundary inclusions
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi a
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I := \{\partial a \hookrightarrow a\}
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski"}> Cisinski, prop. 8.1.31, 8.1.35
            ).
          %h3#model_category_structure_on_presheaves Model category structure on presheaves
          %p
            (…)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+model+structure"} generalized Reedy model structure
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#bergermoerdijk_type Berger-Moerdijk type
          %h4#specific_examples Specific examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
                is a generalized Reedy category, in particular the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            %li
              %p
                Any (finite)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is also a generalized Reedy category, with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mo +
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mo −
                        %mo =
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_+ = G_- = G
            %li
              %p
                Connes’
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cycles"} category of cycles
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Λ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal%27s+category+Gamma"} Segal's category
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            %li
              %p
                The Moerdijk-Weiss
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
                is generalized Reedy. The degree is given by the number of vertices in a tree.
              %p
                See also the discussion at
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+set"} dendroidal set
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            %li
              %p
                Any generalized
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+category"} direct category
                or generalized
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+category"} inverse category
                is also a generalized Reedy category, in which either
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mo −
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_-
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_+
                consists only of the isomorphisms.
          %h4#the_class_of_crossed_group_sites The class of crossed group sites
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+group"}
                  crossed
                  = succeed "-group" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G : S^{op} \to Set
              equipped with
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for each object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S
                  a group structure on
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_s
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi r
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s, r\in S
                  a left
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mi r
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_r
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(s,r)
                  ;
            %p
              such that for all morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi s
                    %mo →
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : s \to r
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo :
                    %mi t
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta : t \to s
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g,h \in G_r
              we have
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %msup
                          %mi α
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                        %mi β
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_*( \alpha \circ \beta)  = g_*(\alpha) \circ \alpha^*(g)_* \beta
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_* (id_r) = id_r
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi α
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi α
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi α
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^* (g \cdot h) = h_*(\alpha)^*(g)\cdot \alpha^*(h)
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi α
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^*(e_r) = e_s
                  ;
            %p
              where
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_*
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_*
              denotes the group action and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi α
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi r
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^* : G_r \to G_s
              the presheaf map.
            %p
              The
              %strong total category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S G
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+group"}
                crossed
                = succeed "-group" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is the category with the same objects as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \to s
              being pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha, g) \in S(s,r)\times G_r
              and with composition defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi β
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\alpha, g) \circ (\beta, h)
                    \=
                    (\alpha \cdot g_*(\beta), \beta^*(g) \cdot h)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BergerMoerdijk11"}> BM11, def. 2.1
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is equipped with a generalized Reedy structure, then an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+group"}
                crossed
                = succeed "-group" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is called
              %strong compatible
              with that generalized Reedy structure if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "-action" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mo +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^+
                  and
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mo −
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^-
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo :
                        %mi r
                        %mo →
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : r \to s
                  is in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mo −
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^-
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G_s
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi α
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^* (g) = e_r
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi α
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi α
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_*(\alpha) = \alpha
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi e
                            %mi s
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = e_s
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi pl
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{pl}
              of planar finite rooted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trees"} trees
              is a strict
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              of non-planar finite rooted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trees"} trees
              is the total category of an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi pl
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{pl}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+group"} crossed group
              which to a planar tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              assigns its group of non-planar automorphisms.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              be a strict
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a compatible
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+group"}
                  crossed
                  = succeed "-group" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S G
              for which the embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi S
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \hookrightarrow S G
              is a morphism of generalized Reedy categories.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BergerMoerdijk11"}> BM11, prop. 2.10
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              A “more generalized” notion is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/c-Reedy+category"} c-Reedy category
            %li
              A more specialized notion is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+category"} Eilenberg-Zilber category
          %h2#references References
          %p Cisinski’s notion of generalized Reedy category appears as def 8.1.1 in
          %ul#Cisinski
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/joyalscatlab/published/Les+pr%C3%A9faisceaux+comme+type+d%27homotopie"} Les préfaisceaux comme modèles des types d'homotopie
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.univ-toulouse.fr/~dcisinsk/ast.pdf"} pdf
          %p The Berger-Moerdijk definition of generalized Reedy category appears in
          %ul
            %li#BergerMoerdijk11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"}> Clemens Berger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %em On an extension of the notion of Reedy category
              %strong 269
              (2011) 977–1004 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0809.3341"}> arXiv:0809.3341
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00209-010-0770-x"} doi:10.1007/s00209-010-0770-x
        .revisedby
